{"authored" [{"question" "q-81025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors are non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-4\\text{i} \\\\ -8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}-4\\text{i} \\\\ -8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-4\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-4\\text{i}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=-4\\text{i}v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-4\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =-2\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =-4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =2\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81025" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =-4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine whether $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ 6-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\text{i} \\\\ -6{\\text{i}}^{2}-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\text{i}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\text{i}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=3\\text{i}v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =3\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38475" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38475" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The eigenvectors are non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{\\text{i}}^{2}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i}(\\text{i}+1) \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(1+\\text{i})[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(1+\\text{i})v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Av=(1+\\text{i})v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =1+\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =1+\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =1-\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ is not an eigenvector of $A$"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =1+\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2+3\\text{i},$\nthen what is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,\\lambda =2+3\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2+3\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3\\text{i} & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(1-3\\text{i}){x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+(-1-3\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-(2+3\\text{i})I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables to be the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}(1+3\\text{i}){x}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}(1+3\\text{i}){x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-2,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=-\\frac{1+3\\text{i}}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1-3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81187" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ be linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nGiven that ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+5\\text{i}$ is an eigenvalue of $A,$ find the value of $\\frac{{a}_{1}{a}_{2}}{{b}_{1}{b}_{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\,{\\lambda }_{1}=1+5\\text{i}$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{\\lambda }_{1}I & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1+5\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1+5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5-5\\text{i} & -5 \\\\ 10 & 5-5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(-5-5\\text{i}){x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}+(5-5\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-(1+5\\text{i})I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\text{i}){x}_{2}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\text{i}){x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-2,$ we get the eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since ${\\lambda }_{1}=1+5\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}=\\overset{―}{{\\lambda }_{1}}=1-5\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, the corresponding eigenvector to ${\\lambda }_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{1}{a}_{2}}{{b}_{1}{b}_{2}}=\\frac{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})}{(-2)(-2)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0aed9f2d60c3511e84d5ff8866713509b9d5a365e5d992dfbf6afbb654d9a514" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140387" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ are linearly independent eigenvectors of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}],$\nwhat is the value of $\\frac{{a}_{1}{a}_{2}}{{b}_{1}{b}_{2}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc7e4296f7f63ff65da5774d1aae950c8ee1d0df86ea0a304b0e58dccd5bec4a" "basis" 1521 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-38480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the eigenvalues of $A.$ To do that, we must solve the characteristic equation $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-6-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-6-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-(-4)(5) & =0 \\\\ -12+6\\lambda -2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+20 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{{4}^{2}-4(1)(8)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$\n\nNow, let's consider the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2+2\\text{i}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{\\lambda }_{1}I & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2+2\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4-2\\text{i} & -4 \\\\ 5 & 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}(-4-2\\text{i}){x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+(4-2\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the matrix $A-(-2+2\\text{i})I$ is singular, the system above must have a non-zero solution. This means that one equation of the system is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as the free variable. For example, from the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=(-1-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}){x}_{1}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ (-1-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}){x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=2,$ we get the eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, to compute the second eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2-2\\text{i}$, we simply compute the complex conjugate of ${\\overset{―}{v}}_{1},$ and get\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}={\\overset{―}{v}}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{1}{a}_{2}}{{b}_{1}{b}_{2}} & =\\frac{(2)(2)}{(-2-\\text{i})(-2+\\text{i})}=\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14041802/state.json" "file_sha256" "b